1
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,962
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:00:56,306 --> 00:00:57,515
‎Man, it's nice and cool in here.

3
00:01:23,124 --> 00:01:24,626
‎Hold on. Why am I avoiding him?

4
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:28,588
‎Gosh, you startled me.

5
00:01:28,671 --> 00:01:29,631
‎Mr. Ma?

6
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:31,674
‎Hello.

7
00:01:33,635 --> 00:01:34,969
‎Where's Yeo-ri?

8
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:41,518
‎EPISODE 10

9
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:52,111
‎Gang-uk.

10
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,250
‎What are you doing here?

11
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:07,794
‎I got on the first flight
‎after we talked last night.

12
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:11,714
‎Wait, you can't…

13
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:13,466
‎We're wearing gloves.

14
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:15,009
‎Let's at least hold hands like this.

15
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:17,554
‎If I see ghosts again, so be it.

16
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:22,600
‎I heard from Ms. Eom
‎that the meeting didn't go well.

17
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:25,687
‎That's right.

18
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:32,152
‎I've been feeling so out of place
‎ever since I got here.

19
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:36,406
‎I can't let you feel that way.

20
00:02:38,074 --> 00:02:39,159
‎Yeo-ri.

21
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:41,494
‎I haven't eaten anything all day
‎and I'm starving.

22
00:02:41,578 --> 00:02:43,079
‎Can we eat before we head back?

23
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:44,372
‎I didn't even eat on the plane.

24
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:47,959
‎We can do that.

25
00:02:48,042 --> 00:02:49,002
‎Let's go.

26
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:51,963
‎What should we eat?

27
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:58,052
‎-Do you like it?
‎-Yeah.

28
00:02:58,636 --> 00:03:01,014
‎-You must've been starving.
‎-Very starving.

29
00:03:03,975 --> 00:03:04,893
‎Here.

30
00:03:05,602 --> 00:03:06,436
‎Thank you.

31
00:03:06,519 --> 00:03:07,353
‎Here you go.

32
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:09,314
‎Can you feed me?

33
00:03:17,155 --> 00:03:20,491
‎It feels like we're eating underwater.
‎This is fun.

34
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:24,871
‎To me, it feels like
‎the fish are watching us eat.

35
00:03:26,164 --> 00:03:27,749
‎That might be how it is for them.

36
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:30,084
‎Oh, right.

37
00:03:33,254 --> 00:03:34,088
‎I brought this.

38
00:03:35,131 --> 00:03:36,341
‎Thank you.

39
00:03:36,424 --> 00:03:38,676
‎I didn't think you'd bring it yourself.

40
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:42,430
‎I was only hoping you'd
‎pass it along to Mr. Bong.

41
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:43,765
‎I'm touched.

42
00:03:43,848 --> 00:03:46,643
‎I couldn't just pass it along
‎when it's something you need.

43
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:52,148
‎You went through all that trouble
‎to bring this to me,

44
00:03:53,024 --> 00:03:54,734
‎but I don't know if I can give it to her.

45
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,445
‎It's not over yet, so let's wait a bit.

46
00:03:58,279 --> 00:03:59,864
‎Hyeong-min might have some good news.

47
00:04:00,782 --> 00:04:01,783
‎Hyeong-min?

48
00:04:01,866 --> 00:04:03,785
‎He's the best at digging up information.

49
00:04:03,868 --> 00:04:06,746
‎I dare say he's better than
‎most intelligence agencies.

50
00:04:08,373 --> 00:04:11,292
‎I also did some digging myself.

51
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:14,712
‎You said Ms. Han seemed averse
‎when you mentioned her family.

52
00:04:16,172 --> 00:04:18,633
‎Her dispute with her brother
‎was more serious than we thought.

53
00:04:18,716 --> 00:04:20,176
‎I found a few articles about them.

54
00:04:25,223 --> 00:04:26,224
‎Hey, Hyeong-min.

55
00:04:26,307 --> 00:04:28,768
‎Mr. Ma, I did some more digging.

56
00:04:28,851 --> 00:04:33,398
‎It looks like Ms. Han posts photos
‎from the same spot after her exhibitions.

57
00:04:33,481 --> 00:04:35,817
‎She's posted similar photos
‎about three times,

58
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:38,194
‎and she just posted another one.

59
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:40,363
‎-Where is that?
‎-It looks like

60
00:04:40,446 --> 00:04:42,865
‎a riverside location in Singapore.

61
00:04:42,949 --> 00:04:46,494
‎There's a bridge in the photos
‎and I looked it up.

62
00:04:46,577 --> 00:04:49,122
‎Turns out, it's a big tourist photo spot.

63
00:04:49,205 --> 00:04:50,373
‎Right, so where is that?

64
00:04:51,791 --> 00:04:53,626
‎I'll send you the photos and coordinates.

65
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:54,961
‎Okay.

66
00:04:55,545 --> 00:04:57,088
‎-I think he found her.
‎-He did?

67
00:04:57,171 --> 00:04:58,047
‎-Yeah.
‎-Oh, Mr. Ma.

68
00:04:58,131 --> 00:04:59,257
‎Yeah?

69
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,634
‎I went down a rabbit hole
‎from her social media account

70
00:05:01,718 --> 00:05:03,594
‎and came across some kind of forum.

71
00:05:03,678 --> 00:05:05,179
‎I'll send that too. Take a look.

72
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:07,015
‎Okay, thanks. I'll have a look.

73
00:05:09,559 --> 00:05:12,103
‎PETITION AGAINST
‎CHAEUM ARTRION'S DESTRUCTION

74
00:05:12,186 --> 00:05:14,272
‎It might be quicker to find this river.

75
00:05:14,355 --> 00:05:15,481
‎Yeah, the river.

76
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:18,651
‎Let's see. Is that a church in the back?

77
00:05:18,735 --> 00:05:22,030
‎-We can compare the buildings.
‎-Okay.

78
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:25,491
‎This building is right here.

79
00:05:25,992 --> 00:05:29,495
‎I think we're around the right place.

80
00:05:30,246 --> 00:05:31,247
‎Over there.

81
00:05:34,208 --> 00:05:35,293
‎Yeah, that's it.

82
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:39,172
‎That's her.

83
00:05:42,133 --> 00:05:43,843
‎-Let's go up to her.
‎-Okay.

84
00:06:05,239 --> 00:06:07,909
‎Why did you come looking for me?

85
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:10,703
‎Will you please hear me out?

86
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:15,792
‎You must think I want to stay on at Reina

87
00:06:16,876 --> 00:06:19,378
‎because I'm reluctant
‎to give up my position as CEO.

88
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:21,881
‎But the true reason I want to stay

89
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:26,052
‎is because of something called Siena Hall.

90
00:06:26,803 --> 00:06:27,637
‎Siena Hall?

91
00:06:28,721 --> 00:06:30,223
‎It's Reina's wedding venue.

92
00:06:30,306 --> 00:06:31,849
‎My dad built it,

93
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:34,644
‎and my mom managed it.

94
00:06:36,145 --> 00:06:38,773
‎They both passed away many years ago,

95
00:06:39,649 --> 00:06:40,983
‎so I always needed

96
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:43,861
‎something to hold on to.

97
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:47,073
‎That was Siena Hall.

98
00:06:48,407 --> 00:06:49,992
‎To me, it's a place

99
00:06:50,576 --> 00:06:53,955
‎that holds the memories
‎I shared with my parents.

100
00:06:55,331 --> 00:06:56,666
‎Just like

101
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,168
‎Chaeum Artrion is to you.

102
00:07:00,586 --> 00:07:01,838
‎I believe I told you

103
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:04,715
‎to leave my family out of this.

104
00:07:05,883 --> 00:07:07,802
‎I hope you don't get the wrong idea.

105
00:07:07,885 --> 00:07:09,846
‎We're only trying to tell you

106
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:13,099
‎that there's a way to solve your problem.

107
00:07:13,182 --> 00:07:14,016
‎My problem?

108
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:18,271
‎I heard your brother took on a huge debt
‎while expanding the business too much.

109
00:07:19,355 --> 00:07:22,859
‎That you might lose Chaeum Artrion
‎to property speculators.

110
00:07:23,568 --> 00:07:25,027
‎Ms. Han,

111
00:07:25,111 --> 00:07:28,281
‎your own father designed
‎and built that space.

112
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:30,616
‎Don't you want to protect it?

113
00:07:36,622 --> 00:07:37,498
‎You're right.

114
00:07:39,083 --> 00:07:41,794
‎My brother inherited the place
‎after our father passed away.

115
00:07:42,962 --> 00:07:44,881
‎It's true that Chaeum Artrion
‎is special to me.

116
00:07:45,381 --> 00:07:49,135
‎I actually tried several times
‎to buy the property myself,

117
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:53,973
‎but they refused to hand it over
‎unless I repaid my brother's debt in full.

118
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,309
‎And because of the legal dispute,

119
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:59,645
‎my brother and I
‎are worse than sworn enemies now.

120
00:08:00,229 --> 00:08:01,647
‎It must've been so tough for you.

121
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:03,357
‎How exactly

122
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:06,777
‎are you saying you can solve this problem?

123
00:08:08,821 --> 00:08:10,072
‎We'll have Chaeum Artrion

124
00:08:10,156 --> 00:08:13,284
‎designated as a nationally registered
‎cultural heritage site.

125
00:08:13,993 --> 00:08:16,204
‎Then regardless of who owns it,

126
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:18,039
‎no one will be able
‎to damage the property.

127
00:08:18,122 --> 00:08:19,040
‎Just a moment.

128
00:08:19,123 --> 00:08:23,085
‎Chaeum Artrion is only 45 years old.

129
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:25,171
‎An asset must be at least 50 years old

130
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:27,882
‎to be nationally registered
‎as cultural heritage.

131
00:08:27,965 --> 00:08:29,634
‎The government recently implemented

132
00:08:29,717 --> 00:08:32,094
‎an Act on the Conservation and Utilization
‎of Modern and Contemporary

133
00:08:32,178 --> 00:08:33,471
‎Cultural Heritage.

134
00:08:33,554 --> 00:08:35,139
‎If an asset would qualify

135
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:38,309
‎for national registration
‎as cultural heritage at 50 years,

136
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:42,313
‎but needs protection now
‎because it's at risk of being damaged,

137
00:08:42,396 --> 00:08:44,732
‎it can be designated
‎as preliminary cultural heritage.

138
00:08:48,778 --> 00:08:49,654
‎If you see here,

139
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:51,864
‎there's already a precedent.

140
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:53,199
‎NOVELIST YUN HAE-SEOK'S "WRITING CHAIR"
‎DESIGNATED PRELIMINARY CULTURAL HERITAGE

141
00:08:55,868 --> 00:08:57,578
‎Do you really think it's possible?

142
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:00,581
‎For it to be designated
‎as preliminary cultural heritage?

143
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:04,001
‎This is how the public reacted
‎when they heard

144
00:09:04,085 --> 00:09:05,836
‎that Chaeum Artrion could become damaged.

145
00:09:07,088 --> 00:09:08,548
‎There are many people

146
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:12,134
‎who'd be heartbroken
‎to see the place run down,

147
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:14,136
‎just like you and me.

148
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:17,181
‎The culture and arts community
‎has already been shedding light on this.

149
00:09:17,807 --> 00:09:19,850
‎If the architecture community
‎backs public opinion,

150
00:09:19,934 --> 00:09:21,310
‎I'm sure it'll be possible.

151
00:09:25,898 --> 00:09:29,151
‎Let's say Chaeum Artrion is designated
‎as a preliminary cultural heritage site.

152
00:09:30,736 --> 00:09:32,029
‎What about after that?

153
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,574
‎The property will still need maintenance.

154
00:09:35,116 --> 00:09:36,284
‎Reina will acquire it.

155
00:09:39,036 --> 00:09:40,955
‎You'll acquire the property?

156
00:09:41,038 --> 00:09:44,125
‎If your brother hands it over
‎to Reina Cultural Foundation

157
00:09:44,208 --> 00:09:46,210
‎instead of selling it
‎to property speculators,

158
00:09:47,295 --> 00:09:50,423
‎we'll conserve and run it
‎as an art and cultural space.

159
00:09:51,048 --> 00:09:54,468
‎Of course,
‎we'd expect you to be in charge.

160
00:10:01,475 --> 00:10:03,894
‎Okay. I understand your point.

161
00:10:03,978 --> 00:10:05,938
‎I must say I'm tempted.

162
00:10:06,731 --> 00:10:07,690
‎But…

163
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:11,652
‎let's say I decide to side with you.

164
00:10:12,236 --> 00:10:15,197
‎How can I be sure that my 3%
‎will be enough for you to win?

165
00:10:16,949 --> 00:10:18,075
‎Three percent.

166
00:10:18,784 --> 00:10:22,204
‎I'll get the papers signed by morning
‎and attend the general meeting.

167
00:10:23,122 --> 00:10:26,792
‎Then Cheon Yeo-ri will
‎no longer have a hold on Reina.

168
00:10:27,710 --> 00:10:28,878
‎I'll see you back in Korea.

169
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:35,092
‎What if

170
00:10:35,176 --> 00:10:37,345
‎something else were to come up

171
00:10:37,428 --> 00:10:39,889
‎and you lose your position
‎at the general meeting?

172
00:10:40,848 --> 00:10:43,267
‎I'd lose my chance to double my investment

173
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:46,354
‎and the hope you gave me
‎to save my father's work.

174
00:10:47,647 --> 00:10:49,857
‎I'm sharing my will and purpose with you.

175
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:51,233
‎Because without will,

176
00:10:52,318 --> 00:10:54,111
‎nothing will ever change.

177
00:10:56,238 --> 00:10:58,616
‎I will make it happen.

178
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:01,285
‎I just need you

179
00:11:02,078 --> 00:11:03,996
‎to side with me this time.

180
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:19,053
‎This is a huge wager for me.

181
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:22,473
‎Give me some time to think.

182
00:11:32,316 --> 00:11:33,150
‎Take this.

183
00:11:33,901 --> 00:11:35,486
‎It's a gift I prepared

184
00:11:36,362 --> 00:11:37,488
‎just for you, Ms. Han.

185
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:42,034
‎I hope you like it.

186
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:50,334
‎Goodbye.

187
00:12:03,514 --> 00:12:05,141
‎She never gave a clear answer.

188
00:12:06,183 --> 00:12:07,977
‎Still, you did your best.

189
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:09,353
‎Let's give it some time.

190
00:12:13,190 --> 00:12:14,442
‎You're worried, aren't you?

191
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:21,073
‎Hey, Hyeong-min.

192
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:23,409
‎Hello? Mr. Ma, did you find the place?

193
00:12:23,492 --> 00:12:25,953
‎Thanks to you,
‎we met her and got to talk to her.

194
00:12:26,036 --> 00:12:27,496
‎Thanks so much.

195
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:30,458
‎If you're grateful,
‎will you bring back some gifts?

196
00:12:30,541 --> 00:12:32,710
‎Investigator Ko is pretty upset

197
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:34,795
‎that you took time off
‎without telling him.

198
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:36,297
‎You're…

199
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:38,591
‎Okay. I'll come back
‎with lots of presents.

200
00:12:38,674 --> 00:12:39,925
‎We'll look forward to it.

201
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:41,594
‎Okay. Thanks.

202
00:12:41,677 --> 00:12:42,595
‎Sure. Have a good…

203
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:47,141
‎-Hyeong-min did a great deal.
‎-He did.

204
00:12:49,101 --> 00:12:51,979
‎Yeo-ri, I need to buy gifts
‎for Hyeong-min and Pil-dong.

205
00:12:52,062 --> 00:12:53,606
‎Can you help me pick them out?

206
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:55,941
‎You have a great eye and sense of style.

207
00:12:56,025 --> 00:12:57,276
‎Pick something for my grandma too.

208
00:12:58,277 --> 00:13:01,197
‎We fly out tomorrow morning,
‎so we have the time, don't we?

209
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:03,407
‎Let's do that.

210
00:13:03,491 --> 00:13:05,159
‎Okay. Let's go.

211
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:06,827
‎I'll buy the presents.

212
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:09,246
‎Nice. I'm going to buy lots of stuff.

213
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:11,624
‎-What's that? It's a palace.
‎-Yeah.

214
00:13:11,707 --> 00:13:13,250
‎The key chains are really pretty.

215
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:15,753
‎I'll buy you one, Yeo-ri.
‎I can afford this much.

216
00:13:15,836 --> 00:13:18,506
‎-These ones…
‎-I want everything from here to here.

217
00:13:21,091 --> 00:13:22,551
‎Wow, look at this mural.

218
00:13:25,137 --> 00:13:27,264
‎Man, this would be perfect for Madam Pang.

219
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:28,390
‎What do you think, Yeo-ri?

220
00:13:30,309 --> 00:13:32,394
‎-Which one looks nice?
‎-How about this one?

221
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:33,938
‎Is it a bit too…

222
00:13:34,021 --> 00:13:35,981
‎One for Pil-dong, and one for Hyeong-min.

223
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:38,651
‎He must want to dress you up.

224
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:48,327
‎-Gosh.
‎-No, this is…

225
00:13:53,165 --> 00:13:53,999
‎What's wrong?

226
00:13:55,417 --> 00:13:56,377
‎That scared me.

227
00:13:56,919 --> 00:13:59,129
‎Don't you think
‎your grandmother would like this?

228
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:00,047
‎For you?

229
00:14:00,130 --> 00:14:02,716
‎I want to wear this at home.
‎I'll get one of these too.

230
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:03,884
‎I love it.

231
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:16,230
‎Aren't you hot, Yeo-ri?

232
00:14:16,313 --> 00:14:17,731
‎How about some ice cream?

233
00:14:21,819 --> 00:14:23,070
‎-I want to try yours.
‎-Yeah?

234
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:25,281
‎Me too.

235
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:32,079
‎-One, two, three.
‎-One, two…

236
00:14:34,373 --> 00:14:35,583
‎Tastes like soy-pickled onions.

237
00:14:53,434 --> 00:14:54,351
‎Put them back.

238
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:55,561
‎Okay.

239
00:14:57,187 --> 00:14:58,355
‎Yeo-ri.

240
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:35,267
‎A noodle place.

241
00:15:35,351 --> 00:15:36,560
‎That one looks good.

242
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:39,980
‎Xiaolongbao and dumplings.

243
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:42,608
‎Man, the chickens here are huge.

244
00:15:42,691 --> 00:15:44,526
‎Do you prefer fried chicken
‎with or without seasoning?

245
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:45,986
‎-With seasoning.
‎-Really?

246
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:47,488
‎We don't match. I prefer it without.

247
00:15:49,323 --> 00:15:51,408
‎Goodness, the prawns are massive.

248
00:15:52,076 --> 00:15:53,744
‎Man, it looks delicious.

249
00:15:56,413 --> 00:15:58,499
‎Yeo-ri, we got everything we ordered.

250
00:15:58,582 --> 00:15:59,541
‎-We did?
‎-Yeah.

251
00:16:00,125 --> 00:16:02,127
‎Gosh, this is a lot of food.

252
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:03,796
‎-Let's stuff our faces tonight.
‎-Okay.

253
00:16:03,879 --> 00:16:05,297
‎You haven't eaten well
‎since you came, right?

254
00:16:06,548 --> 00:16:08,342
‎I have. I've been eating.

255
00:16:08,425 --> 00:16:10,636
‎No, you haven't.
‎Your face is half its size.

256
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:11,887
‎That won't do.

257
00:16:12,554 --> 00:16:14,723
‎This place is known for its skewers.

258
00:16:15,557 --> 00:16:16,976
‎This one. Try it.

259
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:18,394
‎-A skewer?
‎-You said you like seasoning,

260
00:16:18,477 --> 00:16:19,895
‎so make sure to dip it in this.

261
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:28,237
‎I saw this on TV
‎and always wanted to try it.

262
00:16:29,029 --> 00:16:30,072
‎Aren't you glad we came?

263
00:16:31,949 --> 00:16:33,242
‎Let's cheers to that.

264
00:16:34,284 --> 00:16:35,160
‎-Cheers.
‎-Cheers.

265
00:16:37,538 --> 00:16:39,331
‎My gosh, I'm full.

266
00:16:40,290 --> 00:16:41,500
‎I ate too much.

267
00:16:41,583 --> 00:16:43,085
‎-Did you enjoy it?
‎-Yeah.

268
00:16:43,669 --> 00:16:45,212
‎-Did you enjoy it too?
‎-Yes.

269
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:47,673
‎The weather's gotten nicer.

270
00:16:47,756 --> 00:16:49,967
‎It has. I was sweating so much earlier.

271
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:51,343
‎It's not as bad now.

272
00:17:03,856 --> 00:17:04,773
‎This is really nice.

273
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:08,694
‎-Gang-uk.
‎-Yeah?

274
00:17:09,695 --> 00:17:11,405
‎Thank you so much.

275
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:14,074
‎I'm glad you're here

276
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:15,868
‎with me.

277
00:17:15,951 --> 00:17:17,911
‎Gosh, it's the least I can do.

278
00:17:23,042 --> 00:17:26,503
‎Are you really okay? You don't see them?

279
00:17:28,589 --> 00:17:30,758
‎I haven't seen them yet,
‎so I'll probably be fine.

280
00:17:46,857 --> 00:17:48,650
‎What's wrong? Do you see them?

281
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:50,110
‎Yes.

282
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:51,987
‎I think I do.

283
00:17:58,619 --> 00:18:00,079
‎I see nothing but you.

284
00:18:44,873 --> 00:18:47,626
‎I wanted to get a room on the same floor,

285
00:18:47,709 --> 00:18:49,044
‎but they were fully booked.

286
00:18:55,592 --> 00:18:56,510
‎This is my room.

287
00:18:57,845 --> 00:18:58,762
‎This is it?

288
00:18:59,763 --> 00:19:01,932
‎Oh, so this is it.

289
00:19:02,975 --> 00:19:04,810
‎Well… Okay.

290
00:19:04,893 --> 00:19:05,853
‎Well then…

291
00:19:06,645 --> 00:19:08,814
‎Get some rest. I'll be going.

292
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:14,278
‎Want to come in for a cup of tea?

293
00:19:14,361 --> 00:19:15,195
‎Yes.

294
00:19:17,739 --> 00:19:18,907
‎-Come inside.
‎-Okay.

295
00:19:31,253 --> 00:19:32,171
‎Yeo-ri.

296
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:34,965
‎I think you picked out the perfect gift.

297
00:19:35,048 --> 00:19:36,508
‎Madam Pang will love it.

298
00:19:44,808 --> 00:19:45,684
‎What are you thinking about?

299
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:50,856
‎Actually, yesterday…

300
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:53,358
‎I remembered something.

301
00:19:54,318 --> 00:19:55,152
‎About what?

302
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:57,404
‎Before I fell into the water,

303
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:01,325
‎Ji-hwan put a necklace on me.

304
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:04,828
‎He said it was really special to him.

305
00:20:06,747 --> 00:20:08,123
‎But I think I lost it.

306
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:13,045
‎There was something he told me,

307
00:20:14,379 --> 00:20:17,049
‎and I can't get it out of my head.

308
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:20,594
‎Yeo-ri.

309
00:20:21,845 --> 00:20:23,180
‎Don't let it weigh you down.

310
00:20:24,014 --> 00:20:25,349
‎Let's take it slow, one step at a time.

311
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:28,060
‎We made an amazing discovery today anyway.

312
00:20:29,353 --> 00:20:30,229
‎Like what?

313
00:20:31,104 --> 00:20:32,773
‎We can hold hands if we're wearing gloves.

314
00:20:34,274 --> 00:20:36,568
‎Seeing that I don't see any ghosts yet,

315
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:37,861
‎doesn't that mean we're safe?

316
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:39,613
‎I guess so.

317
00:20:40,572 --> 00:20:42,866
‎Why don't you see any ghosts?

318
00:20:44,743 --> 00:20:45,661
‎I wonder why.

319
00:20:48,288 --> 00:20:51,083
‎Maybe if there's something

320
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:54,044
‎between our hands when we touch,

321
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:56,421
‎that makes it okay?

322
00:20:58,507 --> 00:20:59,383
‎Warmth?

323
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:05,222
‎Maybe if we share warmth
‎through our hands,

324
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:07,891
‎that makes you see ghosts too?

325
00:21:08,392 --> 00:21:09,559
‎Could it be that?

326
00:21:13,438 --> 00:21:14,815
‎You have a point.

327
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:16,525
‎Warmth.

328
00:21:31,623 --> 00:21:32,457
‎Yeo-ri.

329
00:21:34,251 --> 00:21:36,837
‎There's something
‎I wanted to tell you for a while now.

330
00:21:37,879 --> 00:21:38,755
‎You know,

331
00:21:39,631 --> 00:21:41,717
‎if it means I can be with you,

332
00:21:43,093 --> 00:21:44,511
‎I don't mind seeing ghosts.

333
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:47,556
‎So from now on…

334
00:21:51,727 --> 00:21:55,147
‎I'm really grateful to you
‎for saying that, Gang-uk.

335
00:21:58,191 --> 00:22:00,110
‎But seeing someone I love

336
00:22:01,862 --> 00:22:03,280
‎suffer because of me…

337
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:05,907
‎isn't what I want.

338
00:23:50,887 --> 00:23:51,721
‎Yeo-ri.

339
00:24:41,521 --> 00:24:42,606
‎What are you doing?

340
00:24:42,689 --> 00:24:43,607
‎You're up.

341
00:24:44,107 --> 00:24:45,442
‎Have a seat. I'm almost done.

342
00:24:58,663 --> 00:25:01,666
‎I figured you wouldn't have eaten
‎Korean food for a few days.

343
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,919
‎I went to the supermarket
‎and these caught my eye.

344
00:25:04,961 --> 00:25:06,004
‎Which one do you want?

345
00:25:07,422 --> 00:25:10,717
‎I'll have this one. The bulgogi flavor.

346
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:13,053
‎You'll have the bulgogi?
‎Okay, then I'll have the kimchi.

347
00:25:15,931 --> 00:25:16,932
‎Thanks for this.

348
00:25:17,015 --> 00:25:18,475
‎Sure. Let's dig in.

349
00:25:20,185 --> 00:25:21,478
‎It looks so good.

350
00:25:31,154 --> 00:25:32,948
‎It tastes like the kimchi we eat in Korea.

351
00:25:33,573 --> 00:25:35,033
‎This tastes like actual bulgogi.

352
00:25:40,997 --> 00:25:42,666
‎It's perfect with cooked rice.

353
00:25:43,833 --> 00:25:45,085
‎It feels like we're having

354
00:25:45,919 --> 00:25:48,088
‎a home-cooked meal together.

355
00:26:07,941 --> 00:26:08,775
‎Where's Ms. Cheon?

356
00:26:08,858 --> 00:26:10,193
‎Her plane just landed.

357
00:26:15,407 --> 00:26:16,241
‎Let's go.

358
00:26:19,494 --> 00:26:21,621
‎AGENDA: MOTION TO REMOVE CEO CHEON YEO-RI

359
00:26:35,552 --> 00:26:36,386
‎Ok Gye-hui.

360
00:26:37,387 --> 00:26:40,223
‎You could barely look me in the eye,

361
00:26:41,016 --> 00:26:42,017
‎and you dare to do this?

362
00:26:42,100 --> 00:26:42,976
‎My goodness.

363
00:26:44,269 --> 00:26:46,688
‎Let's be honest.
‎It wasn't that I couldn't face you.

364
00:26:46,771 --> 00:26:49,357
‎I was only acting on instinct
‎and political acumen.

365
00:26:50,191 --> 00:26:51,568
‎Besides,

366
00:26:51,651 --> 00:26:55,030
‎not all flowers bloom
‎on the first day of spring.

367
00:26:55,822 --> 00:26:59,909
‎I just waited for the right time
‎to come out in full bloom.

368
00:26:59,993 --> 00:27:02,787
‎I believe that day is today.

369
00:27:20,638 --> 00:27:21,514
‎Ma'am.

370
00:27:21,598 --> 00:27:23,933
‎Ms. Han didn't participate
‎in the early electronic vote.

371
00:27:24,017 --> 00:27:26,895
‎She sent a proxy
‎to cast her vote in person today.

372
00:27:29,105 --> 00:27:30,940
‎Yeo-ri, you got this.

373
00:27:31,024 --> 00:27:31,858
‎Okay?

374
00:27:32,692 --> 00:27:33,610
‎You got this!

375
00:27:42,494 --> 00:27:44,662
‎GENERAL MEETING OF SHAREHOLDERS
‎POWER OF ATTORNEY

376
00:27:45,497 --> 00:27:47,624
‎DELEGATOR: SHAREHOLDER HAN SE-IN

377
00:28:13,733 --> 00:28:15,151
‎Hello, everyone.

378
00:28:15,235 --> 00:28:17,904
‎We will now begin the extraordinary
‎general meeting of shareholders

379
00:28:17,987 --> 00:28:19,948
‎regarding the motion for removal
‎of Reina Hotel's CEO, Cheon Yeo-ri.

380
00:28:20,990 --> 00:28:23,493
‎The online electronic vote
‎closed yesterday.

381
00:28:23,576 --> 00:28:25,912
‎A great number of shareholders
‎cast their vote,

382
00:28:25,995 --> 00:28:28,373
‎but as the result is very close,

383
00:28:28,456 --> 00:28:32,836
‎we request those present today
‎who have not yet voted

384
00:28:32,919 --> 00:28:35,088
‎to please vote now.

385
00:28:38,299 --> 00:28:39,259
‎IN FAVOR

386
00:28:40,885 --> 00:28:41,719
‎IN FAVOR

387
00:28:42,846 --> 00:28:43,680
‎OPPOSED

388
00:29:18,923 --> 00:29:19,883
‎In favor.

389
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:21,593
‎Opposed.

390
00:29:22,177 --> 00:29:23,011
‎In favor.

391
00:29:23,636 --> 00:29:24,637
‎In favor.

392
00:29:24,721 --> 00:29:25,847
‎In favor.

393
00:29:28,975 --> 00:29:32,520
‎We will now announce
‎the result of the vote

394
00:29:32,604 --> 00:29:35,315
‎on the motion to remove
‎Reina Hotel's CEO, Cheon Yeo-ri.

395
00:29:36,274 --> 00:29:40,695
‎First is the result of the electronic vote
‎that closed yesterday.

396
00:29:40,779 --> 00:29:44,032
‎There were 51.0% votes
‎in favor of the removal,

397
00:29:44,115 --> 00:29:47,160
‎and 49.0% votes
‎opposed to the removal.

398
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:52,791
‎Next is the result
‎of the on-site vote from today.

399
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:57,003
‎There were 48.5% votes
‎in favor of the removal,

400
00:29:57,086 --> 00:30:00,298
‎and 51.5% votes opposed to the removal.

401
00:30:00,799 --> 00:30:05,512
‎Those opposed to the removal
‎led by 3% points in the on-site vote,

402
00:30:05,595 --> 00:30:07,347
‎so the overall result is…

403
00:30:19,484 --> 00:30:21,319
‎IN FAVOR: 48.5%
‎OPPOSED: 51.5%

404
00:30:21,402 --> 00:30:24,197
‎IN FAVOR: 49.5%, OPPOSED: 50.5%
‎REMOVAL OF CEO CHEON YEO-RI REJECTED

405
00:30:24,280 --> 00:30:26,491
‎Votes in favor, 49.5%.

406
00:30:26,574 --> 00:30:29,410
‎Votes opposed, 50.5%.

407
00:30:30,495 --> 00:30:33,832
‎As a result, the removal
‎of Reina Hotel's CEO, Cheon Yeo-ri,

408
00:30:34,499 --> 00:30:37,252
‎has been officially rejected.

409
00:30:55,353 --> 00:30:56,688
‎How could this be, Mom?

410
00:31:07,323 --> 00:31:10,243
‎Ms. Cheon, congratulations on the win.

411
00:31:11,244 --> 00:31:15,915
‎I must say,
‎our shareholders have a great eye.

412
00:31:15,999 --> 00:31:16,833
‎Don't you think?

413
00:31:18,334 --> 00:31:22,630
‎This just goes to show
‎that Reina Hotel needs you at the helm.

414
00:31:22,714 --> 00:31:25,174
‎We just helped you prove that, didn't we?

415
00:31:26,384 --> 00:31:27,260
‎Excuse us.

416
00:31:29,637 --> 00:31:33,224
‎-You're really something, Director Ok.
‎-Jeez.

417
00:31:33,308 --> 00:31:34,767
‎That was some turnaround.

418
00:31:34,851 --> 00:31:38,229
‎We may have lacked clout,
‎but we never lacked funds.

419
00:31:38,313 --> 00:31:40,106
‎Call your uncle, Gye-dong, right away.

420
00:31:40,189 --> 00:31:41,774
‎We need a contingency plan, fast.

421
00:31:41,858 --> 00:31:43,026
‎Darn it.

422
00:31:57,457 --> 00:31:59,250
‎Thank you for changing your mind

423
00:31:59,834 --> 00:32:00,835
‎at the last moment.

424
00:32:01,836 --> 00:32:03,254
‎I'll keep my promise.

425
00:32:04,213 --> 00:32:05,089
‎I trust you will.

426
00:32:06,966 --> 00:32:10,053
‎I've learned something from this ordeal.

427
00:32:11,012 --> 00:32:12,972
‎However uncomfortable
‎the past or reality is,

428
00:32:13,681 --> 00:32:15,600
‎you must face it head-on to resolve it.

429
00:32:17,852 --> 00:32:21,022
‎Oh, and the gift you left me…

430
00:32:21,773 --> 00:32:22,941
‎Do you like it?

431
00:32:23,524 --> 00:32:26,527
‎One of the hottest keywords
‎on the investment platform

432
00:32:26,611 --> 00:32:29,072
‎you're about to launch is "folk painting."

433
00:32:29,614 --> 00:32:33,451
‎And I noticed you seem to like
‎butterfly-themed folk paintings.

434
00:32:33,534 --> 00:32:37,330
‎It's by an artist named Dowon.
‎I just recently discovered him.

435
00:32:37,413 --> 00:32:39,999
‎I thought you'd appreciate
‎the work's true value.

436
00:32:43,252 --> 00:32:44,587
‎It definitely won me over.

437
00:32:45,213 --> 00:32:47,131
‎It's what sealed the deal for me.

438
00:32:51,344 --> 00:32:52,971
‎CEO KANG MIN-HWAN

439
00:33:20,540 --> 00:33:22,125
‎Thank you for your help with this.

440
00:33:22,959 --> 00:33:26,212
‎I was able to get through it,
‎thanks to you both.

441
00:33:27,588 --> 00:33:30,341
‎I look forward to
‎continuing to work with you.

442
00:33:31,384 --> 00:33:32,260
‎Oh, of course.

443
00:33:41,060 --> 00:33:44,063
‎Here's the slush fund file
‎I mentioned last time.

444
00:33:44,897 --> 00:33:48,860
‎I won't go easy on Director Ok
‎or her people because they're family.

445
00:33:49,527 --> 00:33:51,612
‎We must cut out what is rotten

446
00:33:51,696 --> 00:33:53,614
‎to ensure Reina Group stays healthy.

447
00:34:00,455 --> 00:34:04,292
‎Director Ok of Gallery Cheon sold artworks
‎to Reina Hotel at inflated rates

448
00:34:05,460 --> 00:34:07,462
‎and kept the difference
‎to create a slush fund?

449
00:34:09,756 --> 00:34:12,842
‎Prosecutors are eyeing Director Ok
‎for another matter too.

450
00:34:13,426 --> 00:34:14,761
‎Prosecutors are onto her?

451
00:34:14,844 --> 00:34:16,929
‎Did she bribe a politician or something?

452
00:34:17,013 --> 00:34:18,973
‎Her younger brother,
‎Chief Prosecutor Ok Gye-dong,

453
00:34:19,057 --> 00:34:21,142
‎helped Yeeon Foundation
‎launder money through a painting.

454
00:34:21,225 --> 00:34:24,520
‎It seems it was used to bribe a politician
‎to secure a building license.

455
00:34:24,604 --> 00:34:25,730
‎Which politician is that?

456
00:34:25,813 --> 00:34:28,566
‎It's Assemblyman Park Jin-dong,
‎former pro golfer Park Seung-jae's father.

457
00:34:32,862 --> 00:34:33,905
‎How interesting.

458
00:34:37,492 --> 00:34:38,826
‎Look, Gye-dong.

459
00:34:38,910 --> 00:34:42,163
‎You can't just look out for yourself.

460
00:34:42,246 --> 00:34:45,249
‎Do you know the nightmare
‎I've been living through lately?

461
00:34:46,250 --> 00:34:47,168
‎Gye-hui.

462
00:34:47,251 --> 00:34:49,045
‎I'm in deep trouble as it is.

463
00:34:49,962 --> 00:34:53,091
‎I sided with the wrong guy thanks to you,
‎and I'm about to go down.

464
00:34:53,591 --> 00:34:56,469
‎Man, you told me
‎to side with Park Jin-dong,

465
00:34:56,552 --> 00:34:57,845
‎saying he'd become your in-law.

466
00:34:57,929 --> 00:35:01,808
‎Right, so think of a way
‎to get back at Yeo-ri.

467
00:35:01,891 --> 00:35:03,601
‎Do it like your life depends on it.

468
00:35:03,684 --> 00:35:05,853
‎I need to survive for you to live too!

469
00:35:07,188 --> 00:35:08,731
‎Darn you.

470
00:35:10,108 --> 00:35:11,275
‎He's helpless.

471
00:35:11,359 --> 00:35:14,612
‎I don't know who he takes after
‎to be such a coward.

472
00:35:14,695 --> 00:35:16,739
‎Who's calling now? Don't answer it.

473
00:35:16,823 --> 00:35:18,116
‎It's Min-hwan.

474
00:35:19,367 --> 00:35:20,409
‎Why is he calling?

475
00:35:23,454 --> 00:35:25,289
‎Hello, Mr. Kang.

476
00:35:32,088 --> 00:35:34,090
‎Hey, Pil-dong. I just got back to Korea.

477
00:35:34,173 --> 00:35:36,592
‎Where in Korea?
‎You're not home yet, are you?

478
00:35:36,676 --> 00:35:37,635
‎I'm at the door.

479
00:35:37,718 --> 00:35:41,055
‎Wait. Stop right where you are.
‎Don't you dare open that door.

480
00:35:41,139 --> 00:35:42,849
‎Turn around and come to the office.

481
00:35:42,932 --> 00:35:44,559
‎Why? Did something happen at work?

482
00:35:44,642 --> 00:35:46,811
‎Something's about to happen to you.

483
00:35:46,894 --> 00:35:48,771
‎What could possibly happen to me?

484
00:35:48,855 --> 00:35:50,356
‎I'm tired. I'm going inside to rest.

485
00:35:50,439 --> 00:35:52,108
‎No, you can't do that. Wait.

486
00:35:52,191 --> 00:35:53,985
‎Listen carefully.
‎The moment you step inside,

487
00:35:54,068 --> 00:35:56,779
‎-you will be doomed.
‎-Fine, whatever. Bye.

488
00:35:59,323 --> 00:36:00,241
‎Why you…

489
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:03,411
‎It hurts, it hurts!

490
00:36:06,414 --> 00:36:07,582
‎You damn punk.

491
00:36:08,332 --> 00:36:10,960
‎How could you treat
‎your precious grandson like this?

492
00:36:11,043 --> 00:36:13,337
‎Not even some luggage
‎would deserve this treatment!

493
00:36:13,421 --> 00:36:14,380
‎Then what about you?

494
00:36:15,006 --> 00:36:16,966
‎Think of what you did to me.

495
00:36:17,049 --> 00:36:20,469
‎She was born in the year
‎of the Black Monkey, wasn't she?

496
00:36:21,679 --> 00:36:23,931
‎You even had the nerve
‎to swap out her date of birth?

497
00:36:26,058 --> 00:36:27,310
‎No wonder.

498
00:36:27,393 --> 00:36:28,895
‎I had a feeling something was off.

499
00:36:29,395 --> 00:36:30,980
‎No need to discuss this any further.

500
00:36:31,063 --> 00:36:33,274
‎Thankfully it was an engagement,
‎not a marriage.

501
00:36:33,357 --> 00:36:34,650
‎We'll pretend it never happened.

502
00:36:34,734 --> 00:36:38,029
‎No one calls off an engagement
‎over a birth year these days.

503
00:36:38,112 --> 00:36:39,530
‎If you won't do it, I will!

504
00:36:40,114 --> 00:36:41,699
‎I'll meet with Yeo-ri's grandma
‎and take care of it.

505
00:36:41,782 --> 00:36:43,284
‎No. You can't do that.

506
00:36:43,367 --> 00:36:45,828
‎You can stop me now,
‎but you can't stop me forever.

507
00:36:48,164 --> 00:36:49,957
‎Talk to me about it then.

508
00:36:50,041 --> 00:36:51,834
‎What is the deal with the Black Monkey?

509
00:36:56,547 --> 00:36:58,007
‎Your heart surgery.

510
00:37:02,637 --> 00:37:03,679
‎My heart transplant?

511
00:37:03,763 --> 00:37:05,181
‎Shaman Sim said to me

512
00:37:06,182 --> 00:37:08,684
‎that someone born
‎in the year of the Black Monkey

513
00:37:08,768 --> 00:37:10,645
‎would give you a second lease on life.

514
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:15,107
‎And the one who gave you the heart
‎was born in that very year.

515
00:37:15,691 --> 00:37:17,610
‎-So it's a good thing.
‎-No!

516
00:37:18,611 --> 00:37:22,490
‎The heart beating inside you
‎once belonged to a Black Monkey,

517
00:37:22,573 --> 00:37:25,201
‎so if you were to form a bond
‎with the same Chinese zodiac…

518
00:37:28,412 --> 00:37:31,290
‎it would cut your extension on life.

519
00:37:33,209 --> 00:37:35,836
‎Grandma, it's all superstition.

520
00:37:35,920 --> 00:37:37,505
‎There's no basis to that.

521
00:37:38,172 --> 00:37:41,300
‎I don't believe such superstitions.
‎They don't work on me.

522
00:37:41,384 --> 00:37:42,635
‎I'll give you three days.

523
00:37:43,594 --> 00:37:45,888
‎End it with Yeo-ri by then!

524
00:37:47,014 --> 00:37:47,890
‎Grandma.

525
00:37:49,016 --> 00:37:50,017
‎Grandma.

526
00:37:53,104 --> 00:37:54,689
‎I'm begging you, okay?

527
00:37:55,731 --> 00:37:57,900
‎I really like Yeo-ri.

528
00:37:58,651 --> 00:37:59,568
‎So please

529
00:38:00,194 --> 00:38:02,697
‎give us a chance and see how we do.

530
00:38:04,198 --> 00:38:05,700
‎Don't even dream of it.

531
00:38:07,451 --> 00:38:08,744
‎Oh, my goodness.

532
00:38:12,415 --> 00:38:14,500
‎Oh, good grief.

533
00:38:18,004 --> 00:38:21,007
‎CL Group will help us?

534
00:38:21,090 --> 00:38:24,260
‎It's less help
‎and more an offer to join forces.

535
00:38:24,885 --> 00:38:25,720
‎This is unexpected.

536
00:38:27,263 --> 00:38:28,347
‎Given our situation,

537
00:38:28,931 --> 00:38:32,059
‎those who'd joined forces with us
‎have been cutting us loose.

538
00:38:32,143 --> 00:38:36,564
‎Why would a company as great as CL
‎want to work with us?

539
00:38:36,647 --> 00:38:37,565
‎You're desperate.

540
00:38:38,316 --> 00:38:40,484
‎Nothing motivates people like it.

541
00:38:41,068 --> 00:38:44,363
‎We have no reason
‎to refuse an offer from CL Group.

542
00:38:44,447 --> 00:38:46,991
‎The only title I have is
‎director of an art gallery,

543
00:38:47,074 --> 00:38:50,119
‎and I might not even have that
‎for much longer.

544
00:38:50,202 --> 00:38:52,079
‎We did gain something from the attempt,

545
00:38:52,163 --> 00:38:55,333
‎since we now know
‎the extent of support Yeo-ri can call on.

546
00:38:55,416 --> 00:38:58,669
‎I'm grateful
‎if that's how you decide to see it.

547
00:38:59,337 --> 00:39:02,548
‎So, what will you do if we join forces?

548
00:39:03,174 --> 00:39:04,550
‎Sign a merger with Reina.

549
00:39:08,596 --> 00:39:09,722
‎A merger?

550
00:39:09,805 --> 00:39:12,016
‎If CL were to merge with Reina,

551
00:39:12,099 --> 00:39:14,643
‎it would reshape the entire Asian market.

552
00:39:14,727 --> 00:39:17,688
‎We could create
‎a leading integrated resort complex.

553
00:39:18,272 --> 00:39:19,732
‎That's what I'll achieve.

554
00:39:20,316 --> 00:39:23,444
‎Gosh, just hearing about it
‎creates a grand picture.

555
00:39:23,527 --> 00:39:28,199
‎But Chairwoman Baek and Cheon Yeo-ri
‎would definitely be against it.

556
00:39:28,282 --> 00:39:29,575
‎We'll prepare for that.

557
00:39:29,658 --> 00:39:31,702
‎If Reina's stock price continues to fall,

558
00:39:31,786 --> 00:39:33,621
‎CL Group will buy up
‎as much as we can.

559
00:39:34,205 --> 00:39:35,331
‎Goodness.

560
00:39:35,414 --> 00:39:38,376
‎You're really determined,
‎aren't you, Mr. Kang?

561
00:39:39,752 --> 00:39:42,046
‎I'm just a tad bit intimidated.

562
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:53,849
‎Hey, Yeo-ri?

563
00:39:53,933 --> 00:39:56,352
‎Why are you speaking so quietly?

564
00:39:56,435 --> 00:39:59,438
‎Oh, it's just that my grandma's here.

565
00:40:00,272 --> 00:40:01,357
‎Should I hang up then?

566
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:03,692
‎No, no. Let's talk.

567
00:40:05,694 --> 00:40:06,737
‎Yeo-ri.

568
00:40:06,821 --> 00:40:08,697
‎I like talking on the phone with you,

569
00:40:09,281 --> 00:40:10,199
‎but I miss you.

570
00:40:11,909 --> 00:40:12,743
‎Me too.

571
00:40:13,869 --> 00:40:15,454
‎-Really?
‎-Yeah.

572
00:40:15,538 --> 00:40:16,956
‎I'll come over then.

573
00:40:17,039 --> 00:40:19,208
‎-What?
‎-You said you missed me too.

574
00:40:19,291 --> 00:40:20,501
‎I'll come over.

575
00:40:39,937 --> 00:40:41,564
‎Where are you going this late at night?

576
00:40:41,647 --> 00:40:42,648
‎The convenience store.

577
00:40:55,744 --> 00:40:56,745
‎Gang-uk.

578
00:40:58,038 --> 00:40:58,873
‎Yeo-ri.

579
00:41:01,834 --> 00:41:02,918
‎I missed you so much, Yeo-ri.

580
00:41:05,880 --> 00:41:07,214
‎You actually came over.

581
00:41:07,298 --> 00:41:08,132
‎Of course I did.

582
00:41:11,844 --> 00:41:14,138
‎-Let's go inside.
‎-What? Oh, okay.

583
00:41:14,221 --> 00:41:17,725
‎Gosh, this brings back memories.

584
00:41:18,934 --> 00:41:21,103
‎The day I first came here,

585
00:41:21,187 --> 00:41:23,564
‎the kid I saw in that corner
‎followed me home.

586
00:41:23,647 --> 00:41:25,274
‎To think of how scared I was that day…

587
00:41:27,693 --> 00:41:30,529
‎We've been through so much, haven't we?

588
00:41:31,238 --> 00:41:32,072
‎Exactly.

589
00:41:34,200 --> 00:41:37,244
‎It's such a big house
‎and you live here all alone.

590
00:41:38,621 --> 00:41:39,538
‎Can I…

591
00:41:40,539 --> 00:41:41,832
‎come over often?

592
00:41:48,339 --> 00:41:49,173
‎Yeo-ri.

593
00:41:50,633 --> 00:41:52,885
‎If you had a time machine,
‎when would you travel to?

594
00:41:53,469 --> 00:41:54,512
‎The future? The past?

595
00:41:55,846 --> 00:41:56,680
‎What about you?

596
00:41:57,264 --> 00:41:59,266
‎-I'd go to the future.
‎-Why?

597
00:42:01,810 --> 00:42:05,064
‎I'd like to see what hobbies we share,

598
00:42:05,147 --> 00:42:08,609
‎what we eat at what famous restaurants,
‎and what films we watch together.

599
00:42:09,360 --> 00:42:11,362
‎I'd also like to see
‎the places we travel to,

600
00:42:11,445 --> 00:42:15,282
‎and which parks we go to for walks
‎while holding hands.

601
00:42:15,366 --> 00:42:16,450
‎That's why.

602
00:42:17,493 --> 00:42:18,494
‎What about you?

603
00:42:19,578 --> 00:42:20,704
‎For me…

604
00:42:21,705 --> 00:42:22,665
‎it's the past.

605
00:42:24,250 --> 00:42:26,126
‎To the day it happened.

606
00:42:28,796 --> 00:42:31,173
‎Before I called you earlier,

607
00:42:32,091 --> 00:42:35,511
‎I was looking at some reports
‎about the accident.

608
00:42:40,975 --> 00:42:43,686
‎I found a list of belongings
‎found at the scene,

609
00:42:44,186 --> 00:42:46,272
‎but the pendant isn't there.

610
00:42:46,814 --> 00:42:48,941
‎Oh, the necklace you mentioned?

611
00:42:50,484 --> 00:42:53,904
‎You were definitely wearing it
‎before you fell into the water,

612
00:42:53,988 --> 00:42:55,781
‎but it wasn't found with other belongings.

613
00:42:58,200 --> 00:42:59,118
‎Yeo-ri.

614
00:43:00,077 --> 00:43:01,996
‎According to this incident report,

615
00:43:02,079 --> 00:43:06,083
‎there were paramedics at the scene,
‎as well as your friends.

616
00:43:06,166 --> 00:43:07,960
‎Well, yes.

617
00:43:09,211 --> 00:43:12,047
‎Can we find the person
‎who rescued me that day?

618
00:43:12,131 --> 00:43:14,466
‎They're also civil servants
‎who serve a specific purpose,

619
00:43:14,550 --> 00:43:16,802
‎so we should be able to find them.
‎I'll look into that.

620
00:43:21,807 --> 00:43:23,892
‎Nice one. Straight onto the green.

621
00:43:25,894 --> 00:43:27,563
‎You must play often, Mr. Kang.

622
00:43:28,063 --> 00:43:29,356
‎Only recently.

623
00:43:30,065 --> 00:43:32,610
‎There's talk that a presidential secretary

624
00:43:32,693 --> 00:43:34,820
‎wants to make you
‎the next prosecutor general.

625
00:43:35,321 --> 00:43:36,280
‎Congratulations in advance.

626
00:43:37,323 --> 00:43:38,991
‎No need to get ahead of ourselves.

627
00:43:39,074 --> 00:43:40,743
‎Their opposition is pushing back,
‎as usual.

628
00:43:40,826 --> 00:43:45,080
‎You mean Assemblyman Park Jin-dong,
‎former pro golfer Park Seung-jae's father?

629
00:43:46,915 --> 00:43:48,000
‎You know it all, don't you?

630
00:43:48,083 --> 00:43:50,961
‎I might as well say this
‎since it's just us,

631
00:43:51,045 --> 00:43:53,047
‎but Assemblyman Park is
‎quite something, isn't he?

632
00:43:53,130 --> 00:43:55,549
‎He was a likely presidential candidate,

633
00:43:55,633 --> 00:43:57,468
‎but he lost all hope
‎when his son went down.

634
00:43:57,551 --> 00:44:01,680
‎Now it seems his sole purpose in life
‎is to put allies in important positions.

635
00:44:02,806 --> 00:44:05,059
‎By the way, about Yeeon…

636
00:44:05,684 --> 00:44:06,810
‎Are you going to wait and--

637
00:44:08,479 --> 00:44:09,355
‎Oh, right.

638
00:44:09,938 --> 00:44:12,483
‎One of our guys you mentioned.
‎Ma Gang-uk, was it?

639
00:44:12,566 --> 00:44:13,942
‎Is he giving you trouble?

640
00:44:17,071 --> 00:44:17,988
‎No.

641
00:44:18,489 --> 00:44:20,324
‎I think he's too great a prosecutor.

642
00:44:20,908 --> 00:44:24,787
‎Competent guys like him
‎deserve a promotion or a reward,

643
00:44:24,870 --> 00:44:27,247
‎so they know their work is worthwhile.

644
00:44:32,961 --> 00:44:34,463
‎Hello, this is Ma Gang-uk.

645
00:44:34,546 --> 00:44:37,966
‎I'm looking for a Ji Sun-ho
‎who was a paramedic at the time.

646
00:44:38,050 --> 00:44:39,176
‎Where is he stationed now?

647
00:44:41,762 --> 00:44:43,097
‎Okay. Thank you.

648
00:44:44,723 --> 00:44:45,724
‎Okay.

649
00:44:50,020 --> 00:44:53,941
‎You want to blow up
‎this Yeeon bribery case, don't you?

650
00:44:54,024 --> 00:44:56,652
‎It's a great opportunity,
‎but an actual investigation could harm

651
00:44:56,735 --> 00:44:58,570
‎your right-hand man,
‎Chief Prosecutor Ok Gye-dong.

652
00:44:58,654 --> 00:45:01,323
‎It sounds like
‎you already know everything.

653
00:45:03,367 --> 00:45:06,537
‎To pave the way for the
‎presidential secretary for civil affairs,

654
00:45:06,620 --> 00:45:10,374
‎I need to crush
‎Assemblyman Park Jin-dong for good.

655
00:45:10,874 --> 00:45:13,168
‎It just so happens
‎that Chief Prosecutor Ok's involved.

656
00:45:16,088 --> 00:45:16,964
‎How about

657
00:45:17,965 --> 00:45:19,466
‎you launch the investigation,

658
00:45:19,550 --> 00:45:21,969
‎but target someone else
‎and corner them instead?

659
00:45:22,469 --> 00:45:26,140
‎Well, as long as it's someone
‎we can connect reasonably enough

660
00:45:26,849 --> 00:45:29,059
‎to put alongside Park Jin-dong, why not?

661
00:45:33,897 --> 00:45:36,150
‎How about CEO Cheon Yeo-ri of Reina Hotel?

662
00:45:37,901 --> 00:45:40,529
‎She practically controls Reina Group.

663
00:45:53,584 --> 00:45:55,085
‎Hey, Gang-uk.

664
00:45:55,169 --> 00:45:56,753
‎I spoke to the paramedic from that day.

665
00:45:57,588 --> 00:45:59,256
‎-Really?
‎-Yes.

666
00:45:59,339 --> 00:46:03,343
‎He was transferred to a fire station
‎down south not too long ago.

667
00:46:04,136 --> 00:46:05,762
‎He remembered your accident

668
00:46:05,846 --> 00:46:08,807
‎because it was
‎a rare occurrence at the time.

669
00:46:10,058 --> 00:46:11,477
‎Really?

670
00:46:11,560 --> 00:46:12,936
‎What a relief.

671
00:46:13,020 --> 00:46:16,273
‎Did you ask him about the pendant?

672
00:46:16,356 --> 00:46:17,191
‎Did he remember it?

673
00:46:17,274 --> 00:46:19,026
‎I wasn't able to ask for details.

674
00:46:19,610 --> 00:46:22,488
‎He got injured while on duty recently.

675
00:46:22,571 --> 00:46:25,157
‎He was hospitalized,
‎and I couldn't ask it all over the phone.

676
00:46:25,240 --> 00:46:27,618
‎So I asked if I could pay him a visit,

677
00:46:27,701 --> 00:46:29,036
‎and he willingly agreed.

678
00:46:29,620 --> 00:46:31,246
‎I can take a half-day off tomorrow ‎and ‎go.

679
00:46:32,039 --> 00:46:32,998
‎Okay.

680
00:46:33,790 --> 00:46:36,251
‎Thank you. See you tomorrow.

681
00:46:36,335 --> 00:46:37,961
‎-‎Okay.
‎-Bye.

682
00:46:56,730 --> 00:46:59,024
‎Yeo-ri, it'll be a pretty long drive.

683
00:46:59,107 --> 00:47:00,734
‎Shall we listen to music?

684
00:47:00,817 --> 00:47:02,361
‎-Yes, sounds good.
‎-Okay.

685
00:47:03,570 --> 00:47:06,782
‎Play something to listen to on a drive
‎with someone you like.

686
00:47:17,251 --> 00:47:18,919
‎MUSIC TO LISTEN TO WITH A LOVER

687
00:47:20,170 --> 00:47:21,213
‎I like the sound.

688
00:47:33,767 --> 00:47:35,686
‎They're renovating
‎the hospital parking lot.

689
00:47:35,769 --> 00:47:38,021
‎-It's easier to park here and walk.
‎-Okay.

690
00:47:38,105 --> 00:47:39,606
‎Do you know this area well?

691
00:47:41,233 --> 00:47:43,944
‎I do know it, but I'll explain later.

692
00:47:49,324 --> 00:47:51,159
‎What's wrong?
‎Are you looking for something?

693
00:47:51,743 --> 00:47:53,495
‎No. It's nothing.

694
00:47:53,579 --> 00:47:55,831
‎-It's that way.
‎-Okay.

695
00:47:59,543 --> 00:48:00,794
‎This one's a turtle.

696
00:48:01,378 --> 00:48:03,714
‎The town is really unique.

697
00:48:03,797 --> 00:48:05,882
‎Yes. That's why it's called the art--

698
00:48:09,636 --> 00:48:10,846
‎-Ms. Pang?
‎-No.

699
00:48:10,929 --> 00:48:12,598
‎-My grandma's in Seoul.
‎-Wasn't that Gang-uk?

700
00:48:12,681 --> 00:48:14,683
‎-What? But that's…
‎-Walk to your right.

701
00:48:14,766 --> 00:48:16,351
‎Was I seeing things?

702
00:48:16,935 --> 00:48:18,270
‎Your grandmother…

703
00:48:18,353 --> 00:48:20,272
‎-Does she live here?
‎-Did she?

704
00:48:21,148 --> 00:48:21,982
‎What?

705
00:48:25,819 --> 00:48:26,653
‎What, Grandma?

706
00:48:26,737 --> 00:48:28,947
‎Hey. I know there's no way,

707
00:48:29,031 --> 00:48:30,282
‎but are you in the area?

708
00:48:30,365 --> 00:48:32,618
‎What are you on about? I'm in Seoul.

709
00:48:32,701 --> 00:48:35,245
‎I'm in a meeting with my chief,
‎so I'll call you back.

710
00:48:35,329 --> 00:48:37,414
‎Okay, you do that.

711
00:48:37,497 --> 00:48:39,166
‎-Wait, Gang-uk.
‎-What?

712
00:48:39,249 --> 00:48:41,084
‎You made such a fuss,

713
00:48:41,168 --> 00:48:44,046
‎so I asked Shaman Sim about it again.

714
00:48:44,630 --> 00:48:49,009
‎He said you must never get involved
‎with anyone born in the Black Monkey year.

715
00:48:49,968 --> 00:48:53,597
‎I know very well how much you like Yeo-ri.

716
00:48:53,680 --> 00:48:55,057
‎If you won't do it,

717
00:48:55,140 --> 00:48:58,226
‎I'll go to Chairwoman Baek tomorrow
‎and handle it myself.

718
00:48:58,894 --> 00:49:00,771
‎Talk to Yeo-ri so she understands,

719
00:49:01,355 --> 00:49:03,148
‎and end it without any more trouble.

720
00:49:03,231 --> 00:49:04,274
‎I have to go.

721
00:49:04,358 --> 00:49:05,692
‎Okay. Bye.

722
00:49:17,746 --> 00:49:20,207
‎Gang-uk. What was that…

723
00:49:21,291 --> 00:49:22,751
‎all about?

724
00:49:24,461 --> 00:49:27,547
‎My grandmother cares a lot
‎about birth dates and fortunes,

725
00:49:28,173 --> 00:49:30,759
‎and she told me not to date
‎a Black Monkey.

726
00:49:30,842 --> 00:49:32,928
‎That's pure nonsense. It's not real.

727
00:49:33,804 --> 00:49:35,681
‎But because my grandmother
‎was so worried,

728
00:49:35,764 --> 00:49:39,976
‎I gave her Pil-dong's wife's date of birth
‎before we got engaged.

729
00:49:40,519 --> 00:49:43,230
‎She found out the truth
‎while we were in Singapore,

730
00:49:43,313 --> 00:49:44,981
‎and she got a little upset.

731
00:49:45,649 --> 00:49:47,651
‎Yeo-ri. You don't have to worry.

732
00:49:47,734 --> 00:49:49,903
‎The Shaman Sim my grandma has faith in?

733
00:49:50,445 --> 00:49:51,988
‎Nothing he says is accurate.

734
00:49:52,072 --> 00:49:54,491
‎He said I'd pass the bar on my second try,
‎but I passed in one go.

735
00:49:55,492 --> 00:49:58,245
‎And the real reason my grandma is angry

736
00:49:58,870 --> 00:50:00,455
‎has nothing to do with your birth year.

737
00:50:01,331 --> 00:50:03,959
‎She's upset that I lied to her.

738
00:50:04,668 --> 00:50:07,671
‎It was my doing, so I'll sort it out.

739
00:50:07,754 --> 00:50:10,215
‎Then we should visit her today

740
00:50:10,298 --> 00:50:12,926
‎to explain everything and apologize.

741
00:50:13,635 --> 00:50:14,511
‎Okay.

742
00:50:14,594 --> 00:50:17,806
‎Let's finish our business first,
‎then go visit her.

743
00:50:18,807 --> 00:50:19,683
‎Let's go.

744
00:50:19,766 --> 00:50:20,726
‎Jeez.

745
00:50:28,358 --> 00:50:32,779
‎ANDONG MIRAE HOSPITAL

746
00:50:33,780 --> 00:50:34,656
‎I think that's him.

747
00:50:37,409 --> 00:50:38,285
‎Hello.

748
00:50:44,082 --> 00:50:46,710
‎You're the lady I rescued back then?

749
00:50:46,793 --> 00:50:48,670
‎Yes. I owe you my life.

750
00:50:49,212 --> 00:50:50,046
‎Thank you very much.

751
00:50:50,130 --> 00:50:52,007
‎Oh, please. It makes my work worthwhile.

752
00:50:53,216 --> 00:50:56,219
‎So what's the pendant
‎you mentioned on the phone?

753
00:50:56,303 --> 00:50:57,512
‎Oh, right.

754
00:50:57,596 --> 00:50:59,890
‎I don't have a photo of it,

755
00:51:00,682 --> 00:51:03,894
‎so I drew what it looked like.

756
00:51:06,062 --> 00:51:07,856
‎Do you remember seeing it?

757
00:51:14,154 --> 00:51:16,114
‎Oh, I remember it.

758
00:51:19,075 --> 00:51:21,244
‎Someone asked for it back then.

759
00:51:23,163 --> 00:51:25,999
‎A lot was going on
‎and the site was a bit chaotic,

760
00:51:26,500 --> 00:51:28,502
‎but I vaguely remember the voice.

761
00:51:29,252 --> 00:51:30,378
‎I'll take it.

762
00:51:30,879 --> 00:51:31,838
‎I'm family.

763
00:51:31,922 --> 00:51:32,881
‎Very well.

764
00:51:41,014 --> 00:51:42,307
‎He said he'd take it.

765
00:51:44,226 --> 00:51:45,435
‎He said he was family.

766
00:51:47,312 --> 00:51:48,647
‎He was family?

767
00:51:49,648 --> 00:51:51,525
‎Who there could've been family?

768
00:51:52,734 --> 00:51:54,361
‎SECRETARY EOM

769
00:51:55,946 --> 00:51:57,781
‎-Excuse me for a moment.
‎-Sure.

770
00:51:58,949 --> 00:52:00,200
‎Hello, Ms. Eom. What is it?

771
00:52:08,834 --> 00:52:09,751
‎We have an exclusive report.

772
00:52:09,835 --> 00:52:11,169
‎Assemblyman Park Jin-dong

773
00:52:11,253 --> 00:52:13,797
‎and Yeeon Museum of Art
‎are implicated in a bribery scandal,

774
00:52:13,880 --> 00:52:17,342
‎with circumstantial evidence linking them
‎to Cheon Yeo-ri, the CEO of Reina Hotel.

775
00:52:17,425 --> 00:52:18,844
‎It's causing unrest in the community.

776
00:52:18,927 --> 00:52:21,179
‎Reina Group and Assemblyman Park Jin-dong

777
00:52:21,263 --> 00:52:26,726
‎had close business ties
‎and even discussed a marriage alliance

778
00:52:26,810 --> 00:52:31,439
‎until Park's son, ‎Park ‎Seung-jae,
‎was ‎detained ‎on ‎suspicion ‎of ‎murder.

779
00:52:31,523 --> 00:52:34,693
‎During the process ‎of ‎obtaining
‎a business license,

780
00:52:34,776 --> 00:52:37,821
‎CEO Cheon of Reina Hotel
‎contacted ‎Yeeon Museum of Art‎…

781
00:52:37,904 --> 00:52:38,822
‎What's going on here?

782
00:52:40,240 --> 00:52:41,741
‎It's obviously fake news.

783
00:52:41,825 --> 00:52:43,285
‎That's right.

784
00:52:43,368 --> 00:52:45,662
‎I know some things about the Yeeon case,

785
00:52:45,745 --> 00:52:48,248
‎and I confirmed
‎that Reina Hotel wasn't involved.

786
00:52:49,207 --> 00:52:50,709
‎Call an emergency meeting

787
00:52:50,792 --> 00:52:52,294
‎and get the legal team
‎for a contingency plan.

788
00:52:52,377 --> 00:52:53,670
‎Yes, ma'am.

789
00:52:53,753 --> 00:52:55,755
‎I'll return to my office and look into it.

790
00:52:57,048 --> 00:52:59,175
‎Don't worry too much. It's not even true.

791
00:53:02,929 --> 00:53:04,973
‎What's going on?
‎You said Reina wasn't involved.

792
00:53:05,056 --> 00:53:07,017
‎I have no clue.
‎I'm here because of that.

793
00:53:07,100 --> 00:53:09,185
‎It's my case,
‎and I'm hearing stuff I didn't know about.

794
00:53:09,269 --> 00:53:12,105
‎Go to your own chief.
‎Why would you come to me?

795
00:53:12,188 --> 00:53:15,609
‎-You know all there is to know here.
‎-Right.

796
00:53:15,692 --> 00:53:17,402
‎Tell me everything you know.

797
00:53:21,656 --> 00:53:23,533
‎It looks like Chief Prosecutor Ok Gye-dong

798
00:53:23,617 --> 00:53:26,786
‎helped Yeeon Museum of Art
‎launder a painting.

799
00:53:27,495 --> 00:53:30,707
‎And Yeeon used that painting
‎to bribe someone to get a license.

800
00:53:30,790 --> 00:53:32,918
‎I know that much. Who did they bribe?

801
00:53:34,210 --> 00:53:35,503
‎Assemblyman Park Jin-dong.

802
00:53:35,587 --> 00:53:38,423
‎Then Ok Gye-dong's name
‎should be on the news, not Reina.

803
00:53:38,506 --> 00:53:41,176
‎He still doesn't know
‎how things work here.

804
00:53:41,259 --> 00:53:43,637
‎Our priority is to protect our own.

805
00:53:43,720 --> 00:53:46,181
‎We don't like anything
‎that makes us look bad.

806
00:53:46,264 --> 00:53:47,974
‎What kind of nonsense…

807
00:53:48,058 --> 00:53:49,225
‎Do you think I'll just sit back?

808
00:53:49,309 --> 00:53:51,519
‎Don't get so worked up about it.

809
00:53:51,603 --> 00:53:53,188
‎Aren't you engaged to Reina Hotel's CEO?

810
00:53:53,897 --> 00:53:55,732
‎If you get too hot-headed and involved,

811
00:53:55,815 --> 00:53:58,109
‎people will question
‎the integrity of the investigation.

812
00:53:58,652 --> 00:53:59,945
‎Oh, right.

813
00:54:00,028 --> 00:54:02,447
‎I was going to ask you anyway.

814
00:54:02,530 --> 00:54:05,909
‎You made some nice connections
‎right after your engagement to an heiress.

815
00:54:05,992 --> 00:54:07,285
‎One word from that pal

816
00:54:07,369 --> 00:54:09,663
‎and our district chief
‎did you a huge favor.

817
00:54:10,872 --> 00:54:12,374
‎Who's that pal and what's the favor?

818
00:54:13,166 --> 00:54:14,793
‎You've been reassigned

819
00:54:14,876 --> 00:54:17,796
‎to an overseas training program
‎you applied for last year.

820
00:54:17,879 --> 00:54:20,256
‎I applied last year and got rejected.

821
00:54:20,340 --> 00:54:22,133
‎Why would they send me now?

822
00:54:22,217 --> 00:54:24,970
‎You didn't know?
‎That pal praised you to no end.

823
00:54:25,053 --> 00:54:26,346
‎What pal?

824
00:54:36,314 --> 00:54:38,191
‎We need to stop the stocks from falling.

825
00:54:38,274 --> 00:54:41,903
‎Yes. We'll make a statement
‎before the market opens tomorrow.

826
00:54:41,987 --> 00:54:45,031
‎The message from the emergency meeting
‎will be sent to all shareholders,

827
00:54:45,115 --> 00:54:46,992
‎and we'll protect our stock price
‎at all costs.

828
00:54:47,075 --> 00:54:47,909
‎Good.

829
00:54:52,122 --> 00:54:54,332
‎You two can come back after you've eaten.

830
00:54:54,833 --> 00:54:55,792
‎Ma'am.

831
00:54:56,376 --> 00:54:57,252
‎Perhaps you could join?

832
00:54:58,503 --> 00:55:00,714
‎You haven't been eating much lately.

833
00:55:02,007 --> 00:55:04,134
‎Yes. Why don't you join us?

834
00:55:05,885 --> 00:55:08,596
‎Well… Sure, why not?

835
00:55:08,680 --> 00:55:09,639
‎Here we go.

836
00:55:13,018 --> 00:55:16,062
‎I'll show you how to eat this.

837
00:55:17,022 --> 00:55:18,606
‎You wrap a piece in kimchi

838
00:55:19,733 --> 00:55:21,109
‎and eat it in one bite.

839
00:55:22,819 --> 00:55:23,862
‎Thank you.

840
00:55:23,945 --> 00:55:25,947
‎Oh, I didn't know
‎you could wrap it like that.

841
00:55:26,656 --> 00:55:27,490
‎Let me try it.

842
00:55:31,077 --> 00:55:32,829
‎-It's spicy.
‎-It's nice and savory.

843
00:55:33,955 --> 00:55:35,915
‎-It's spicy.
‎-It's savory.

844
00:55:35,999 --> 00:55:38,668
‎You don't know your flavors.
‎This is spicy.

845
00:55:38,752 --> 00:55:39,919
‎The tripe is savory.

846
00:55:41,004 --> 00:55:42,422
‎Ma'am, what do you think?

847
00:55:44,591 --> 00:55:45,842
‎Well, it's…

848
00:55:46,426 --> 00:55:47,260
‎It's tasty.

849
00:55:47,343 --> 00:55:49,512
‎See? She said it's spicy.

850
00:55:51,848 --> 00:55:56,186
‎It would be nice
‎if we could eat together like this again.

851
00:55:57,604 --> 00:55:58,563
‎Let's do this again.

852
00:56:01,357 --> 00:56:02,275
‎Sure.

853
00:56:03,318 --> 00:56:05,987
‎-It's nice and spicy.
‎-It's nice and savory.

854
00:56:25,632 --> 00:56:26,508
‎Gang-uk!

855
00:56:45,026 --> 00:56:46,111
‎Why aren't you asleep yet?

856
00:56:49,906 --> 00:56:51,825
‎Are you all right, Gang-uk?

857
00:56:52,408 --> 00:56:53,451
‎What's wrong?

858
00:56:53,535 --> 00:56:54,869
‎It's all good if you're okay.

859
00:56:55,787 --> 00:56:56,704
‎Bye now.

860
00:57:13,680 --> 00:57:17,142
‎Please protect my Gang-uk.

861
00:57:18,184 --> 00:57:20,937
‎Please protect and help him.

862
00:57:21,563 --> 00:57:22,647
‎Please watch over him.

863
00:57:34,075 --> 00:57:34,993
‎Ma.

864
00:57:37,745 --> 00:57:38,830
‎Where'd he go?

865
00:57:44,210 --> 00:57:45,587
‎INCOMING CALL

866
00:57:45,670 --> 00:57:46,921
‎He left his phone.

867
00:57:49,007 --> 00:57:50,550
‎-Hey, Gang-uk.
‎-‎Oh.

868
00:57:50,633 --> 00:57:52,135
‎Is this Ms. Cheon?

869
00:57:53,761 --> 00:57:54,596
‎Yes.

870
00:57:54,679 --> 00:57:58,558
‎It's me, Im Seo-hyeon.
‎It looks like Ma went out.

871
00:58:00,226 --> 00:58:02,770
‎Is that so? Then I'll call again later.

872
00:58:03,438 --> 00:58:05,523
‎By the way…

873
00:58:05,607 --> 00:58:08,318
‎You know he was assigned overseas, right?

874
00:58:09,694 --> 00:58:10,528
‎What?

875
00:58:11,029 --> 00:58:11,946
‎Gang-uk is

876
00:58:12,614 --> 00:58:13,823
‎going abroad?

877
00:58:13,907 --> 00:58:15,992
‎Oh, I guess he hasn't told you yet.

878
00:58:18,536 --> 00:58:22,081
‎I'm not sure if I should tell you this,

879
00:58:22,165 --> 00:58:26,169
‎but this overseas assignment
‎feels a bit fishy.

880
00:58:26,794 --> 00:58:27,962
‎What do you mean?

881
00:58:28,546 --> 00:58:32,967
‎Ever since your scandal blew up,
‎he's been under pressure from higher-ups.

882
00:58:33,801 --> 00:58:36,429
‎I think their goal
‎is ‎to chase Ma out of Seoul.

883
00:58:38,765 --> 00:58:42,310
‎I'll tell him that you called
‎when he comes back.

884
00:58:43,436 --> 00:58:44,270
‎Okay.

885
00:58:58,993 --> 00:59:00,286
‎You have a visitor.

886
00:59:07,252 --> 00:59:08,378
‎Ma'am.

887
00:59:18,513 --> 00:59:19,347
‎Yeo-ri.

888
00:59:20,390 --> 00:59:21,307
‎Yes, ma'am.

889
00:59:22,559 --> 00:59:24,352
‎I really like you.

890
00:59:25,436 --> 00:59:26,563
‎Why?

891
00:59:27,313 --> 00:59:29,399
‎Because Gang-uk likes you.

892
00:59:31,651 --> 00:59:32,986
‎But…

893
00:59:34,696 --> 00:59:38,449
‎I don't think
‎you and Gang-uk are meant to be.

894
00:59:44,122 --> 00:59:45,164
‎Ma'am.

895
00:59:46,499 --> 00:59:50,169
‎If this is about my birth year…

896
00:59:50,253 --> 00:59:51,087
‎That's right.

897
00:59:53,214 --> 00:59:55,758
‎I don't mind if you think
‎I'm an old woman acting silly.

898
00:59:56,342 --> 00:59:57,468
‎But I was told

899
00:59:58,177 --> 00:59:59,721
‎you two are a bad match.

900
01:00:00,763 --> 01:00:02,390
‎Wouldn't it be best to avoid the worst?

901
01:00:04,559 --> 01:00:07,687
‎If you don't mind me saying so,

902
01:00:07,770 --> 01:00:09,856
‎when you talk about
‎the year or date of birth,

903
01:00:11,649 --> 01:00:15,653
‎isn't that just an old,
‎traditional belief?

904
01:00:16,487 --> 01:00:21,618
‎Could you reconsider your beliefs
‎just this once?

905
01:00:21,701 --> 01:00:22,535
‎Sure.

906
01:00:23,244 --> 01:00:25,747
‎It could be a superstition
‎that people made up.

907
01:00:27,123 --> 01:00:28,541
‎But Yeo-ri.

908
01:00:29,208 --> 01:00:31,502
‎In all the years I've lived,

909
01:00:32,420 --> 01:00:35,006
‎there's one thing I know to be true.

910
01:00:36,174 --> 01:00:39,093
‎It's that my ominous hunch
‎was never wrong.

911
01:00:42,263 --> 01:00:43,973
‎Please, I'm begging you.

912
01:00:45,224 --> 01:00:49,187
‎Gang-uk will never leave you,
‎even if his life is at stake.

913
01:00:51,481 --> 01:00:53,399
‎I need you to let him go…

914
01:01:01,866 --> 01:01:03,284
‎I'm sorry.

915
01:01:05,244 --> 01:01:08,289
‎Gang-uk was born with a weak heart.

916
01:01:09,666 --> 01:01:12,168
‎He's had many close calls with death.

917
01:01:14,462 --> 01:01:16,714
‎He found a donor and had surgery,

918
01:01:17,465 --> 01:01:20,301
‎and that's the only reason
‎he's still alive.

919
01:01:21,427 --> 01:01:26,140
‎I can't go on living
‎if something were to happen to him.

920
01:01:29,519 --> 01:01:33,398
‎I know he was in a bad car accident
‎a few months ago.

921
01:01:34,732 --> 01:01:35,983
‎Weren't you with him

922
01:01:36,609 --> 01:01:38,986
‎when that happened too?

923
01:01:52,917 --> 01:01:55,002
‎You can call me a senile old woman.

924
01:01:56,963 --> 01:01:59,924
‎So please…

925
01:02:02,051 --> 01:02:04,345
‎Do me this favor.

926
01:02:29,036 --> 01:02:31,748
‎PROSECUTOR MA

927
01:02:44,343 --> 01:02:46,763
‎The call cannot be connected. You will be‎…

928
01:03:06,908 --> 01:03:10,912
‎Ma'am, the prosecutors' office
‎has sent you a summons notice.

929
01:03:12,580 --> 01:03:15,082
‎Perhaps you could contact Prosecutor Ma--

930
01:03:15,166 --> 01:03:16,083
‎No.

931
01:03:17,418 --> 01:03:18,711
‎Don't tell him.

932
01:03:20,213 --> 01:03:21,547
‎I'll take care of it.

933
01:03:24,091 --> 01:03:25,092
‎All right.

934
01:03:48,866 --> 01:03:51,577
‎I don't mind if you think
‎I'm an old woman acting silly.

935
01:03:52,453 --> 01:03:55,706
‎You two are a bad match.
‎Wouldn't it be best to avoid the worst?

936
01:03:57,500 --> 01:03:59,836
‎Gang-uk was born with a weak heart.

937
01:03:59,919 --> 01:04:03,047
‎That's the only reason he's still alive.

938
01:04:09,887 --> 01:04:11,180
‎-Damn you.
‎-Are you okay, Yeo-ri?

939
01:04:24,902 --> 01:04:27,864
‎If it means I can be with you,

940
01:04:28,948 --> 01:04:30,491
‎I don't mind seeing ghosts.

941
01:04:39,876 --> 01:04:40,877
‎Yeo-ri.

942
01:04:43,462 --> 01:04:46,007
‎Why are you so hard to reach?
‎Do you know how worried I was?

943
01:04:52,555 --> 01:04:53,389
‎Yeo-ri?

944
01:04:59,312 --> 01:05:01,314
‎I should've taken better care of you.

945
01:05:03,357 --> 01:05:04,483
‎It's tough, isn't it?

946
01:05:05,067 --> 01:05:05,985
‎Gang-uk.

947
01:05:10,406 --> 01:05:11,324
‎Should we…

948
01:05:15,286 --> 01:05:16,329
‎break up?

949
01:05:21,167 --> 01:05:22,209
‎Let's call off the engagement.

950
01:06:16,430 --> 01:06:18,808
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

951
01:06:18,891 --> 01:06:21,143
‎Is that more important
‎than your grandson's feelings?

952
01:06:21,227 --> 01:06:22,687
‎It's all for your sake.

953
01:06:22,770 --> 01:06:24,814
‎No, you did it for your own peace of mind.

954
01:06:27,108 --> 01:06:30,111
‎Your stocks are plummeting.
‎Do you have any plans to step down?

955
01:06:30,194 --> 01:06:31,445
‎Since when was it?

956
01:06:31,529 --> 01:06:32,738
‎When did you start targeting Reina?

957
01:06:32,822 --> 01:06:34,198
‎Does it matter when it all started?

958
01:06:34,281 --> 01:06:35,825
‎What we do next is what counts.

959
01:06:35,908 --> 01:06:38,077
‎Given all the evidence,
‎I don't think there will be a way out.

960
01:06:38,160 --> 01:06:40,204
‎Did that bastard
‎Ma Gang-uk blow the whistle?

961
01:06:40,287 --> 01:06:41,622
‎Take responsibility for what you did.

962
01:06:41,706 --> 01:06:43,541
‎Do you remember the yacht incident
‎from 12 years ago?

963
01:06:43,624 --> 01:06:44,542
‎Let's meet up.

964
01:06:44,625 --> 01:06:45,960
‎Who's there?

965
01:06:47,545 --> 01:06:48,379
‎Yeo-ri?

966
01:06:48,963 --> 01:06:53,843
‎Subtitle translation by: Jennifer Jean Lim
